Hamnix Micro feather-nrf52840 size patch to fs/hvfs.ad.
Applied by scripts/mkroot.sh in build/feather-nrf52840/root only; the
committed file is unchanged.

Reason: the nRF52840 has 256 KiB of RAM for everything: kernel data, kernel
stacks and heap, the files in / and every running program's stack and data
(boards/feather_nrf52840/link.ld; programs' code stays in flash).

    snapshot of a directory listing (kernel heap, while the directory is
    open)                                    8 KiB -> 2 KiB
/ has at most 32 entries here (the tmpfs patch) and /bin 13 names; an 8 KiB
block is often not to be had from a heap of about 34 KiB that also holds
the kernel stacks and pipe buffers of a running pipeline.

    open files, system-wide                  64 -> 32 (the table: 3.5 KiB
                                             -> 1.75 KiB of static data)
At most 16 processes run here, and a process started by the shell shares
its three standard descriptors' entries with the shell.  The 1.75 KiB go to
the kernel heap, which milestone 5's namespace tables would otherwise have
made smaller than it was.

Only constants, array lengths, and messages that quote them change.
Generated by editing a copy and
    diff -u --label a/fs/hvfs.ad --label b/fs/hvfs.ad fs/hvfs.ad <copy>

--- a/fs/hvfs.ad
+++ b/fs/hvfs.ad
@@ -143,9 +143,9 @@
 DEV_ZERO: int32 = 3
 
 VFS_NR_FDS: uint32 = 16             # per thread (Hamnix: 64 per task)
-VFS_NR_OPEN: uint32 = 64            # system-wide open files
+VFS_NR_OPEN: uint32 = 32            # Hamnix Micro feather-nrf52840: was 64
 VFS_PATH_MAX: uint32 = 256
-VFS_DIRBUF: uint64 = 8192
+VFS_DIRBUF: uint64 = 2048          # Hamnix Micro feather-nrf52840: was 8192
 
 QTDIR: uint32 = 0x80
 DMDIR: uint32 = 0x80000000
@@ -164,7 +164,7 @@
     aux1: uint64
 
 
-ofiles: Array[64, OpenFile]
+ofiles: Array[32, OpenFile]
 fs_lock: Mutex
 vfs_ready: uint32 = 0
 fat_mounted: uint32 = 0
